A||||4||Coop88||Sway bar size||||5||
Z||000000||Coop88||02-13-2001||12:40 AM||||I've searched for the sizes of the front and rear sway bars(stock) on the 88s. So far, I found two people who thought the rear swaybar was 7/8. Nothing on the front yet. Does anyone know for sure, or where I could find out? Reason I'm asking is I'm trying to redo my suspension with poly, and the guy at energysuspension needs to know. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||02-13-2001||10:33 AM||||I'm pretty sure the front is 1&1/8"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-13-2001||10:47 AM||||On 88's the front is about 1 inch and the rear is about 7/8. The reason I say "About" is because they are actually listed in millimeters but I don't remember the size.<BR>Actually all WS6 Fiero's have the fronts the same size. I think the regular coupes have a 7/8 size bar in front. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coop88||02-13-2001||06:14 PM||||Thanks for the info. I measured my sway bars with this thing I got at Lowe's(cheap). Turns out my rear bar really is 7/8(22.22mm?) and my front bar measured exactly between 1and1/16 and 1and1/8(about 30-31mm?). ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-13-2001||06:20 PM||||According to my fancy 88 press guide, the front bar is 28 mm as opposed to 22 on previous models, and the rear bar is 22mm.<P>Thats factory documented...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||3
